# memokit hook messages (English). Sourced by lib/common.sh.
# Contract: MK_T_<KEY>="template"; %s placeholders; @TAG@ = project tag; %% for a literal percent.
MK_T_TEST_ECHO="[@TAG@] test %s"
MK_T_CONFIG_INVALID="[@TAG@] .claude/memokit.json is invalid (field: %s). The guards deny every Edit/Write/Bash call until it is fixed, so fix .claude/memokit.json by hand in an editor, or set MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1 under env in .claude/settings.local.json and start a new session to fix it there (remove the override afterwards)."
MK_T_CONFIG_NO_JQ_STATIC="jq not found; memokit cannot read .claude/memokit.json. Install jq (e.g. brew install jq). Emergency override: MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1."
MK_T_GE_EMPTY_STDIN_STATIC="Empty stdin received; the PreToolUse payload could not be read, so the file path cannot be classified, denying to be safe. Verify that tools like jq/cat are on PATH, or in an emergency disable with MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1."
MK_T_GE_JQ_FAILED_STATIC="The jq -n call failed; the actual deny reason cannot be shown, but denying to be safe. Emergency override: MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1."
MK_T_GE_INVALID_JSON="The PreToolUse payload is not valid JSON; the file path cannot be classified, denying to be safe. Emergency override: MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1."
MK_T_GE_ROOT_UNKNOWN="Could not determine the repo root (ROOT=%s); the file path cannot be safely classified, denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_READLINK_MISSING="readlink not found; the symlink cannot be resolved, denying to be safe. Install readlink or, in an emergency, disable with MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1."
MK_T_GE_SYMLINK_LOOP="Symlink chain exceeded the 40-hop limit (may be a loop, path=%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_SYMLINK_TARGET_UNREADABLE="Could not read the symlink target (readlink failed or returned empty, path=%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_SYMLINK_DIR_UNRESOLVED="Could not resolve the symlink's containing directory (%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_NORMALIZE_FAILED="Could not normalize the file path (%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_TR_MISSING="tr not found; case normalization cannot be performed, denying to be safe. Install tr (e.g. brew install coreutils) or, in an emergency, disable with MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1."
MK_T_GE_GUARDED_DIR_LOWER_FAILED="Could not lowercase a guarded dir name (tr failed, guardedDir=%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_GUARDED_DIR_LOWER_EMPTY="Could not lowercase a guarded dir name (empty result, guardedDir=%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_PATH_LOWER_FAILED="Could not lowercase the path (tr failed, NORM_PATH=%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_PATH_LOWER_EMPTY="Could not lowercase the path (empty result, NORM_PATH=%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_ROOT_LOWER_FAILED="Could not lowercase the root directory (tr failed, ROOT=%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_ROOT_LOWER_EMPTY="Could not lowercase the root directory (empty result, ROOT=%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_PARENT_DIR_LOOP="Could not find an existing ancestor directory (iteration limit exceeded, path=%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_PARENT_PHYS_FAILED="Could not resolve the ancestor directory's physical path (%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_INODE_LOOP="The inode identity comparison exceeded the iteration limit (path=%s); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_SUBAGENT_CHECK_FAILED="Could not distinguish subagent from main session (jq failed); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_PATH_EXTRACT_FAILED="Could not extract the file path from the payload (jq failed or produced no output); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_CMD_EXTRACT_FAILED="Could not read the Bash command from the payload (jq failed); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GE_WRITE_DENIED="Writing under %s is blocked in the main session (WORKING-MODEL.md §1). Start a subagent with the Agent tool, subagent_type:\"memokit:coder\" (Sonnet), let it do the work and review its output. Emergency override: MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1. (Path: %s -> %s)"
MK_T_GE_BASH_WRITE_DENIED="Writing under %s via Bash is blocked in the main session (WORKING-MODEL.md §1). This is a barrier against habitual violations, not a shell parser -- a determined bypass (base64, a separate script, python -c ...) is still possible. Start a subagent with subagent_type:\"memokit:coder\" (Sonnet). Emergency override: MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1. (Target: %s -> %s, command: %s)"
MK_T_GS_EMPTY_STDIN_STATIC="Empty stdin received; the PreToolUse payload could not be read, so subagent authority cannot be checked, denying to be safe. Verify that tools like jq/cat are on PATH, or in an emergency disable with MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1."
MK_T_GS_JQ_FAILED_STATIC="The jq -n call failed; the actual deny reason cannot be shown, but denying to be safe. Emergency override: MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1."
MK_T_GS_INVALID_JSON="The hook payload is not valid JSON; subagent authority cannot be checked, denying to be safe."
MK_T_GS_SUBAGENT_CHECK_FAILED="Could not distinguish subagent from main session (jq failed); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GS_TOOL_NAME_EXTRACT_FAILED="Could not read tool_name (jq failed); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GS_CMD_EXTRACT_FAILED="Could not read the Bash command (jq failed); denying to be safe."
MK_T_GS_NO_DELEGATION="A subagent may NOT hand its work off to ANOTHER agent (WORKING-MODEL.md §1, memokit:coder rule 0). Do the work yourself; if you cannot, REPORT what you could not do and return -- the orchestrator decides."
MK_T_GS_COMMIT="A subagent may NOT commit (WORKING-MODEL.md §1). Leave the changes in the working tree and report back -- the orchestrator makes the commit, because it must verify the git status and tests ITSELF first. Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_MERGE="A subagent may NOT merge (WORKING-MODEL.md §1). This rule exists because work landed on master before the user ever saw it. Leave the changes on the branch/in the tree and report back. Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_PUSH="A subagent may NOT push (memokit:coder rule 0). It cannot change the remote in any way -- including remote branch DELETION (--delete). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_REBASE="A subagent may NOT rebase (memokit:coder rule 0). It rewrites history. Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_RESET="A subagent may NOT reset (memokit:coder rule 0). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_BRANCH_SWITCH="A subagent may NOT switch to / create a branch (memokit:coder rule 0: 'checkout <other-branch>'). To back out an experiment, reverse the edit by hand (memokit:coder rule 0) -- never restore files through git. Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_STASH="A subagent may NOT use stash (it can permanently lose a parallel subagent's work). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_CHERRY_PICK="A subagent may NOT cherry-pick (it changes history, memokit:coder rule 0). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_CLEAN="A subagent may NOT run 'git clean' (it permanently deletes untracked files). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_TAG_DELETE="A subagent may NOT delete a tag (memokit:coder rule 0). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_REF_DELETE="A subagent may NOT delete a ref (git update-ref -d, memokit:coder rule 0). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_WORKTREE_REMOVE="A subagent may NOT remove a worktree (memokit:coder rule 0). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_BRANCH_DELETE="A subagent may NOT delete a branch (WORKING-MODEL.md §1). Branch cleanup is done by the orchestrator. Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_REVERT="A subagent may NOT run 'git revert' (it creates a commit, WORKING-MODEL.md §1). Back the change out by hand and report back. Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_PULL="A subagent may NOT run 'git pull' (it merges or rebases the remote into the branch and can create commits, memokit:coder rule 0). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_AM="A subagent may NOT run 'git am' (it turns patches into commits, WORKING-MODEL.md §1). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_FILTER_BRANCH="A subagent may NOT run 'git filter-branch' (it rewrites history, memokit:coder rule 0). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_COMMIT_TREE="A subagent may NOT run 'git commit-tree' (it creates commit objects, WORKING-MODEL.md §1). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_BRANCH_FORCE="A subagent may NOT force-move or rename a branch ('git branch -f/-m/-M', memokit:coder rule 0). Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_GS_GH_PR_MERGE="A subagent may NOT merge a pull request ('gh pr merge', WORKING-MODEL.md §1). Leave the changes on the branch and report back. Blocked command: %s"
MK_T_IR_RULES_BASE="[@TAG@-RULE] 1) Never write code under %s in the main session -- open Agent(subagent_type:memokit:coder), then verify it YOURSELF (git status + run the tests yourself). 2) Decision point (dependency | schema | wire contract | security | hard-to-reverse architecture) -> STOP, write your recommendation WITH RATIONALE, suggest a council if you're torn, ASK THE USER. 3) Every choice gets a recommended option + rationale; no neutral list. 4) When the work is done, update docs/STATE.md + commit. 5) Don't claim what you haven't measured: don't call it done if tests aren't green, verify a subagent's report yourself (WORKING-MODEL.md §3). 6) If you don't know the right skill, search with find-skills."
MK_T_IR_RULES_BASE_STATIC="[@TAG@-RULE] Main session must NOT write code under guarded dirs, use the memokit:coder subagent. STOP at a decision point and ask the user. Don't claim what you haven't measured."
MK_T_IR_HINT_DEBUGGING=" [SKILL] Bug hunt -> superpowers:systematic-debugging: hypothesis + evidence first, then the fix."
MK_T_IR_HINT_DECISION=" [SKILL] Decision/architecture -> superpowers:brainstorming first. A hard-to-reverse or uncertain decision -> suggest a council (llm-council) to the user, run it once APPROVED; record the result in docs/DECISIONS.md."
MK_T_IR_HINT_REVIEW=" [SKILL] Before delivery -> /code-review or superpowers:requesting-code-review; we don't call it done without evidence."
MK_T_IR_HINT_HANDOFF=" [SKILL] Handoff -> /memokit:handoff: PRINT the handoff table, verify it by measuring; only if it passes, say, along with the measured output, \"Handoff is up to date — just say 'continue' in the next session.\""
MK_T_IR_HINT_RESUME=" [SKILL] resume -> /memokit:resume: don't re-read STATE if it was already injected; if a THINK-FIRST stamp is present, don't start implementing, ask with your recommendation."
MK_T_IR_HINT_GRAPHIFY=" [SKILL] Codebase question -> graphify (if graphify-out is missing, set it up first with /graphify)."
MK_T_IR_HINT_GRAPHIFY_FRESH=" [SKILL] Codebase question -> graphify. %s"
MK_T_SS_INIT_HINT="(memokit) memokit is not configured in this repo. The user can set it up with /memokit:init if they want -- don't run it on your own, no obligation to even suggest it."
MK_T_SS_HEADER="[%s — session start]"
MK_T_SS_HEALTH_SKIPPED="[@TAG@] Health script not configured or not found -- skipped."
MK_T_SS_DOCS_HEADER="Docs to watch:"
MK_T_SS_HISTORY_NOTE="Do NOT read docs/HISTORY.md (unless searched for)."
MK_T_SS_RESUME_NOTE="If the user says 'resume', use /memokit:resume."
MK_T_SS_MISSING="[@TAG@] Missing files (referenced in config, not found in repo): %s"
MK_T_SS_UNKNOWN_KEYS="[@TAG@] Unknown field(s) in memokit.json: %s -- ignored."
MK_T_SS_CONFIG_INVALID="[@TAG@] .claude/memokit.json is invalid (field: %s). Fix it by hand (the guards deny edits until then; emergency override: MEMOKIT_GUARD_OFF=1 under env in .claude/settings.local.json, then a new session); STATE is still shown below."
MK_T_SS_FALLBACK_STATIC="[memokit] WARNING: automatic STATE.md injection failed (jq did not run). Read docs/STATE.md by hand."
MK_T_SS_STATE_UNREADABLE="[@TAG@] docs/STATE.md could not be read."
MK_T_SS_RISK_SECRET="[@TAG@-SECURITY] %s's permission rules contain a plaintext secret pattern (%s). Remove the value, rotate the secret, and use a keychain/env var instead."
MK_T_SS_RISK_BROAD="[@TAG@-SECURITY] %s has an overly broad permission: %s. Narrow it."
MK_T_ST_NO_GIT="[@TAG@-WARNING] git command not found on PATH; the docs/STATE.md freshness check (whether %s changed, whether commits are behind STATE.md) could not be verified. Do not confuse this with 'not a git repo' -- add git to PATH or check docs/STATE.md by hand."
MK_T_ST_DIRTY="%s has %s uncommitted change(s) but docs/STATE.md was not updated. "
MK_T_ST_BEHIND="%s has %s commit(s) since STATE.md's last update (threshold %s) -- STATE.md was committed but is stale. "
MK_T_ST_TAIL="[@TAG@-WARNING] %sUpdate STATE.md before finishing the work (WORKING-MODEL.md §4) or run /memokit:handoff."
MK_T_CB_AUTONOMOUS="[@TAG@-CONTEXT] Session context is ~%sk tokens, budget %sk. Every turn resends the whole context, so the per-turn cost keeps growing. DO NOT ASK THE USER — YOU decide the handoff timing: (a) finish the work at hand, then /memokit:handoff — when the work will wrap up in a few more turns, or leaving it unfinished would cause an expensive re-orientation in the new session; (b) /memokit:handoff right now — when the remaining work is long, you are at a natural stopping point, or continuing would push the context into the next band. Tell the user your choice and reasoning in ONE LINE (information, not a question). Carry out the handoff completely and verify it BY MEASURING (WORKING-MODEL.md §3). Only once every measurement passes — and not before — say the following, along with the measured output: \"Handoff is up to date — just say 'continue' in the next session.\" If a measurement fails, fix it and re-measure; if you cannot fix it, do not say \"up to date\", report plainly what failed. If an architectural or hard-to-reverse decision comes up, ask the user for their call with your own recommendation (WORKING-MODEL.md §2)."
MK_T_BG_BAD_JSON="[@TAG@-SUBAGENT-BG] payload is not valid JSON, skipping background task check."
MK_T_BG_OWNERSHIP_FAILED="[@TAG@-SUBAGENT-BG] transcript ownership check failed (jq exit %s), skipping background task check (fail-open)."
MK_T_BG_COUNTER_DIR_FAILED="[@TAG@-SUBAGENT-BG] could not create the counter directory (%s), skipping background task check (fail-open)."
MK_T_BG_COUNTER_DATA_FAILED="[@TAG@-SUBAGENT-BG] could not build the counter data, skipping background task check (fail-open)."
MK_T_BG_COUNTER_WRITE_FAILED="[@TAG@-SUBAGENT-BG] could not write the counter file (%s), skipping background task check (fail-open)."
MK_T_BG_BLOCK="[@TAG@-SUBAGENT-BG] You are returning while background work you started is still running:
%s
A report written before it finishes is not evidence. Do not return yet.
For a Bash task: wait for it in the FOREGROUND with one Bash call whose timeout parameter is 600000,
looping until its output file shows it finished (the file path was in the tool result that started it).
For a Monitor task (no output file): run its wait condition in the foreground the same way, or stop
it with TaskStop. Then read the result and finish your report. TaskOutput is not available to subagents.
If it is a server or watcher you no longer need, stop it with TaskStop (ToolSearch \"select:TaskStop\").
Next time pass timeout: 600000 on the Bash call so a normal run stays in the foreground; 600000 is a
cap, not a guarantee, so a run can still end up backgrounded -- if that happens, wait for it before
returning, the same way."
MK_T_BG_LAST_BLOCK="This is the last block. If you still cannot wait, stop the task with TaskStop and make the first
line of your final report: [@TAG@-SUBAGENT-BG] UNFINISHED: %s"
MK_T_PC_SUMMARY="Make sure this summary preserves: the active phase and slice, the SINGLE next step, open blockers and decisions made, recent commits, whether docs/STATE.md is up to date (and if not, what is missing). Drop the detailed historical narrative, repeated tool output, and closed intermediate steps -- the historical record is kept in docs/HISTORY.md."
